  "description": "JUSRIB crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C104 H84 Gd4 N12 O16 S6,C2 H3 N1. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd1B (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd2B (Gd) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.587-3.894 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.13-111.80°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd4(acac)4(L)6(μ3-OH)2]·CH3CN (C106H87Gd4N13O16S6). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
